# =====================================================================
# Release V108 -- cancellation_reason_id GUID (real Dentally shape)
# =====================================================================
# Real Dentally appointment_cancellation_reason_id is a GUID; Bronze.Appointments typed it INT, so
# TRY_CAST(... AS INT) nulled every real GUID -> no cancellation reason ever resolved for real
# tenants (fk_Cancellation_Reason = -1). The reason LOOKUP was fine all along
# (Bronze.Cancellation_Reasons.ID + Gold.Dim_Cancellation_Reasons.bk are varchar GUIDs; the Gold
# join is string-based) -- the appointment's reason column was the only break.
#
# MIGRATE swaps Bronze.Appointments.Appointment_Cancellation_Reason_ID int->varchar(50) IN PLACE
# (Fabric can't ALTER COLUMN type; table is DROP/CREATE -> in-place add/drop/rename preserves data).
# DEPLOY updates the Bronze load to keep the GUID as text (was cast to int). Bronze.Appointments.Table.sql
# is also updated to varchar in the repo for fresh onboarding, but NOT deployed here (DROP/CREATE would
# wipe the existing 247k-row table).
#
# The V108b backfill then TRUNCATEs the appointments for any tenant still in the pre-fix state
# (cancellations but zero reasons), resetting the per-tenant Bronze watermark so the next ingest
# cold-pulls the full history incl cancelled + GUID reasons. Guarded/idempotent: a no-op where already
# fixed (dev). *** You MUST trigger build_Ingest_Dentally (affected tenants) AFTER this deploy *** --
# the manifest can't run the Fabric ingest notebook. Verified on dev: 31,256 cancelled / 21,059 reasons.
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V108__cancellation_reason_guid.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

MIGRATE  Migrations\V108__cancellation_reason_guid.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Bronze.usp_Load_Appointments.StoredProcedure.sql
MIGRATE  Migrations\V108b__reingest_appointments.sql

TEST
